  "notes": "Adds allocation-free current/previous Twin connection diagnostics: discovery/subscription phases, config and peer-state writes, matched configuration ACK, and terminal/abort state. BLEHANDSHAKE DUMP reads the fixed snapshot without a control lease or radio pause. Local write acceptance remains distinct from peer acknowledgment. Existing connection timeout, recovery, search routing and output-control policies are unchanged.\n\nThis investigation distinguishes a long-running configured-link loss from a later initial configuration timeout. Neither establishes the root cause by itself. The diagnostics let the next real occurrence identify the stalled phase without hiding legitimate loss indications.\n\nVerification includes production-code host checks, existing BLE regressions and the ESP32-S3 build. A separate installed-683 QA session completed three active-fault Help/QR paths, one IR and one thermistor primary action and 88 curtain transition frames; it did not establish physical component repair, real load operation or optical acceptance. Full-device QA remains open.\n",
